  "question": {
    "text": "The correct statement(s) related to processes involved in the extraction of metals is(are)<br />&nbsp;",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "VO7z6",
      "text": "Roasting of Malachite produces Cuprite<br />&nbsp;",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JtBsC",
      "text": "Calcination of Calamine produces Zincite<br />&nbsp;",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "UxtzX",
      "text": "Copper pyrites is heated with silica in a reverberatory furnace to remove iron<br />&nbsp;",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "Z5rW7",
      "text": "Impure silver is treated with aqueous <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>KCN</mi></math> in the presence of oxygen followed by reduction with zinc metal",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The ore Calamine contain&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>ZnCO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>. The Calamine on heating produces&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ZnO</mi></math>.<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>ZnCO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mo>&#8710;</mo></mover><mi>ZnO</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p>Cyanide process, also called Macarthur-forrest Process, method of extracting silver from impure&nbsp;ores by dissolving them in a dilute solution of sodium cyanide in the presence of oxygen. The complex formed in the above process reduced to silver metal by the treatment with zinc.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>Ag</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>NaCN</mi><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mrow></mrow></mover><mi>Na</mi><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Ag</mi><msub><mfenced><mi>CN</mi></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>NaOH</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mi>Na</mi><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Ag</mi><msub><mfenced><mi>CN</mi></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>Zn</mi></mover><msub><mi>Na</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Zn</mi><msub><mfenced><mi>CN</mi></mfenced><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>Ag</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>SiO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>​&nbsp;(Silica) is a flux material. It removes impurities as slag. Here, slag consists of Iron in Sulphide ore of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Cu</mi></math>, here impurity is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>FeO</mi></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>FeO</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>SiO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mrow></mrow></mover><msub><mi>FeSiO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math></p><p>Malachite green is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CuCO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>.</mo><mi>Cu</mi><msub><mfenced><mi>OH</mi></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and cuprite is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Cu</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>. The ore malachite green on heating gives cupric oxide but not cuprous oxide.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CuCO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>.</mo><mi>Cu</mi><msub><mfenced><mi>OH</mi></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mo>&#8710;</mo></mover><mn>2</mn><mi>CuO</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math></p>",
    "image": null
